              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "వదులుకో — vadulukō — \"to let go of; to give up\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అతను ఆ ఉద్యోగం కోసం తన చదువు వదులుకున్నాడు. atanu ā udyōgaṁ kōsaṁ tana caduvu vadulukunnāḍu. He gave up his studies for that job."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): వదులుకున్నాను, vadulukunnānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "వదులు, to let loose, + -కో: to let a thing go from oneself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "వదులుకో (vadulukō) is native Dravidian: DEDR 5243 lists Telugu vadalu, \"to leave, to abandon, to let loose\"; -కో, from konu, \"to take\" (DEDR 2151), turns it back on the doer."
            }
          ]
